 Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(3)-f(-5)}{3-(-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{3+5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complete sentence is as follows:\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that ${f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{3}{8}.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3a41212c7a38beab938478a00354b0b6afd96caed552d8eac50ca7b498a56b85" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(c)=-\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{3}{8}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{5}{8}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{8}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{3}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for $f(x)=5\\sqrt{x}-2$ on the interval $[4,9].$\n\n$c=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[4,9]$ and differentiable on $(4,9),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (4,9)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=4$ and $b=9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(9)-f(4)}{9-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(5\\sqrt{9}-2)-(5\\sqrt{4}-2)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{13-8}{5} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\sqrt{x}-2)=\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{c}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{c}} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{c} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ c & ={(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} \\\\ c & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3a41212c7a38beab938478a00354b0b6afd96caed552d8eac50ca7b498a56b85" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345063" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345063" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{25}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,3]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,3],$ the function must be continuous on $[-1,3]$ and differentiable on $(-1,3).$\n\nFirst, notice that the function $h(x)$ is continuous on $[-1,3]$ and differentiable on $(-1,3),$ so it satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nLet's check each of the other functions individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Hence, $f(x)$ is not continuous on $[-1,3].$ Therefore, $f(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $p(x)$ is continuous on $[-1,3]$ but has a corner point at $x=2.$ Hence, $p(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=2,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(-1,3).$ Therefore, $p(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $r(x)$  has a vertical asymptote at $x=-1.$ Hence, $r(x)$  is not continuous on $[-1,3].$ Therefore, $r(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $t(x)$ is continuous on $[-1,3]$ but has a corner point at $x=0.$ Hence, $t(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=0,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(-1,3).$ Therefore, $t(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8df4a86e095daad9a95b1e58d910b1c9f43e98bc9b2f2c326fcdeda5f40dc2f" "basis" 1532 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77888" "field"