re, $r(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $s(x)$ has a corner point at $x=0.$ Hence, it is not differentiable on $(-2,2).$ Therefore, $s(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $p(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Hence, it is not differentiable on $(-2,2).$  Therefore, $p(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f716d7354f66ba6857898b997d23a4d7cd2bed7f6a5f768d2ef0e67da15e37c"} {"question" "q-127009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f390378c1221a74f9572acd1218f2dc69830ecf8932ab444c1ccc83ee35204d2"} {"question" "q-127009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f716d7354f66ba6857898b997d23a4d7cd2bed7f6a5f768d2ef0e67da15e37c"} {"question" "q-127009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/2eba8ffb2094fab214cdebc0459ac6849c6bc2c37ac0f9bbd3fe026e44334800.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/5f439fc57fa9cccf4471379d0b5a4901cdc4fd0ccd997fe9ae2e52d7c0372b94.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/83fffb6e46362e577cdc45bff6123555e070dc539505522ff134f